#X text 600 1056 -> back into input inlet 2 (64-sample loop delay), f 30;
#X obj 850 96 cnv 1 420 330 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 870 122 UNTRAINED BUT ALIVE: the weights are random. A random recurrent network driven by inputs is a RESERVOIR (echo state networks \, Jaeger 2001 \, liquid state machines \, Maass 2002): a rich \, slightly unpredictable echo of its inputs. Reservoir computing trains only a final readout \, here YOU are the readout - by ear., f 56;
#X text 870 233 THE SHAPE of an autoencoder (5 -> 1 -> 5) squeezes everything through one latent neuron. Untrained \, it is not a VAE (lesson 11 shows a real one) \, but the bottleneck still makes all outputs depend on one shared value - nudge it., f 56;
#X text 870 314 FEEDBACK through [s~]/[r~] arrives one block (64 samples) later. In lesson 9 that delay was avoided \, here it is part of the instrument: it turns the network into a resonating \, sometimes chaotic system., f 56;
#X obj 850 436 cnv 1 420 230 empty empty INPUTS:\ sine\ LFO\ rate\ (Hz)\ +\ noise\ per\ input 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
